body:
We tend to use a standardized theme cache struct for things like this. Example in the header:

```cpp
	struct ThemeCache {
		Color valid_color;
		Color warning_color;
		Color error_color;
	} theme_cache;
```

You can then use it as `theme_cache.property` within the C++ file. Even if there's one property, this ensures future properties are also added to it to encourage theme caching.
